# The Berry phase and the spin one-half double cover. Carry a quantum state slowly around a loop and it returns with a
# geometric phase set by the loop, a holonomy. For a spin one-half the phase is half the angle turned, so a physical
# rotation by a quarter turn advances the spinor by an eighth of a full phase cycle, an eighth root of unity. This file
# MODELS the spinor phase as the eight-element cycle of those eighth roots and DEFINES the quarter-turn as the step around
# it. It then PROVES the double cover: eight quarter-turns, a physical rotation by two full turns of four pi, return the
# spinor to itself, while four quarter-turns, a single physical turn of two pi, send it not home but to the opposite phase,
# the minus-one. So a spin one-half needs TWO full rotations to come back, and one rotation flips its sign, the defining
# fact of a spinor and the reason fermions are what they are. The minus-one phase is shown to square to the identity.
# Every theorem is quantified over the actual eight-element phase type and checked by induction.

# The eight spinor phases, the eighth roots of unity a spin one-half passes through as it is rotated. Phase turn-zero is
# plus one, turn-four is minus one, the halfway phase reached after a single physical rotation.
form spinor
  case turn-zero
  case turn-one
  case turn-two
  case turn-three
  case turn-four
  case turn-five
  case turn-six
  case turn-seven

# A physical quarter turn advances the spinor phase by one eighth, stepping around the eight roots.
task quarter
  take a, like spinor
  like spinor
  fork case, read a
    case turn-zero
      send back
        make turn-one
    case turn-one
      send back
        make turn-two
    case turn-two
      send back
        make turn-three
    case turn-three
      send back
        make turn-four
    case turn-four
      send back
        make turn-five
    case turn-five
      send back
        make turn-six
    case turn-six
      send back
        make turn-seven
    case turn-seven
      send back
        make turn-zero

# THE DOUBLE COVER: eight quarter turns, a rotation by two full turns of four pi, return every spinor phase to itself,
# quarter applied eight times is the identity, for all a. So the spinor has period four pi, not two pi. Proved by
# induction over the eight phases.
rule spinor-returns-after-two-full-rotations
  seat a, like spinor
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call quarter
        call quarter
          call quarter
            call quarter
              call quarter
                call quarter
                  call quarter
                    call quarter
                      read a
      read a
  fold a

# ONE ROTATION FLIPS THE SIGN: four quarter turns, a single physical rotation by two pi, send plus one, turn-zero, to
# minus one, turn-four, not back to itself. This is the spinor sign flip under a two pi rotation, the heart of the double
# cover.
rule one-rotation-sends-plus-to-minus
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call quarter
        call quarter
          call quarter
            call quarter
              make turn-zero
      make turn-four
  calm hold

# THE MINUS-ONE SQUARES TO ONE: applying the two pi rotation twice, four quarter turns from minus one, returns to plus
# one, so minus one times minus one is one, the order-two element at the center of the cover.
rule the-minus-one-phase-squares-to-one
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call quarter
        call quarter
          call quarter
            call quarter
              make turn-four
      make turn-zero
  calm hold
